 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**If you mean today, Saturday, October 17, there’s normally no school to skip in Kuala Lumpur.** If your kids have a Saturday class or activity, I’d keep them out of **outdoor** activities: the noon Malaysian API readings were **163 in Cheras and 161 in Batu Muda**, both in the *unhealthy* range. ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/en/))\n\nFor their **next school day**, don’t decide from today’s reading alone. Check the latest reading for the area around their school and the school’s notice. The current reported education guidance calls for outdoor school activities to stop above API 100 and schools to close at API 200; parents concerned about a child’s health may notify the school and keep the child home. That’s especially reasonable if your child has asthma, breathing symptoms, or a lot of outdoor exposure on the journey or at school. ([malaymail.com](https://www.malaymail.com/news/malaysia/2026/10/15/moe-reverts-to-haze-plan-schools-shut-at-api-200-outdoor-classes-at-100-parents-may-keep-kids-home/239253))",
